foreign  [Music]  this is your Tech news briefing for  Tuesday November 22nd I'm Zoe Thomas for  The Wall Street Journal  having hearing problems instead of using  hearing aids you might be able to get  away with just using airpods  that's according to a study published  last week in the journal eye science the  study found that a new pair of Apple  airpods Pro may help some people hear  almost as well as using traditional  hearing aids that could be good news for  anyone struggling with their hearing and  for Apple which has been working on  making inroads in the health space  joining us to discuss the study and its  limits is our Medical Science reporter  Dominique mossbergen hi Dominique thanks  for joining me hi Zoe how are you I  you know can you start by telling us  what came out of this study you know  what is it about airpods that make them  so useful for people struggling with  their hearing  so the study found that airpods Pro with  Apple's live listen function which is  this feature that allows you to use an  external device like an iPhone or an  iPad to pick up external sounds so for  example if you're having a conversation  with someone in a noisy place the idea  is that you can use your phone put it on  the table and direct the mic from your  phone towards that person and the phone  will pick up the sound it'll be filtered  through a program and you'll hear it  through your air pods and through that  it's supposed to be able to filter out  kind of background noise so you can hear  that sound that you're trying to amplify  better and what the study found was that  airpods Pro using this live listen  function was almost as good as two  different kinds of hearing aids at  helping people with mild to moderate  hearing loss to hear speech better and  also in lab tests it was pretty  comparable as some hearing assist of  devices so airpod Pros aren't actually  hearing aids but there were some  features that made them useful for  people with hearing loss what were those  as you said they're not hearing aids and  actually in the study the co-authors  made it really clear that they tested  airpods not as hearing aids but compared  them to something called the personal  sound amplification product or psaps  which is another type of hearing  assistive technology that it's similar  to hearing aids and that their personal  wearables that help amplify sound but  they're not quite as advanced as hearing  aids but the study found that airpod Pro  was able to function as well as other  peace apps the airpod pro was really  good at making the world louder and  therefore helping some people with  hearing loss to hear better  so have less of our grandparents saying  you know speak up young person maybe  that's what the airpods can do right  exactly  are there limitations to using airpods  if you're trying to compensate for some  of your hearing loss yes definitely the  hearing loss experts I've spoken to and  also the study authors themselves make  it really clear that airpods aren't  going to work for everyone who has  hearing loss it's really only going to  be good for people with certain kinds of  hearing loss and also people with more  mild hearing loss also airpods you know  have limited battery life and so they'll  only last for a few hours at a time  before needing to be recharged so you  know it's not something that you can  wear all day also because of how the  airpod pros work and how they work to  amplify an external sound is you need  another device to pick up those external  sounds so for example if you're having a  conversation with someone and you want  to hear them better you'll have to take  your phone out and direct the microphone  towards that person and so that might be  kind of inconvenient when you're walking  around the world and wanting to hear the  world but better or wanting to hear you  know conversations or maybe someone  approaching from behind you or hear a  car coming or something like that you  need to have your phone out at all times  trying to pick up all this sound and  that can be maybe a bit challenging I  want to broaden this out a little bit  because this summer The Food and Drug  Administration did approve some hearing  aids to be sold over the counter what  has that meant for the broader hearing  aid Market yeah I mean it sounds like  that decision by the FDA has been a real  game changer for the market hearing aids  in general are quite expensive they can  cost several thousand dollars they are  not usually covered by insurance  and so it's quite inaccessible to a lot  of people and in fact the FDA has said  that for people under the age of 69 the  number of people who could benefit from  hearing aids only a tiny fraction of  them actually use hearing aids even  though they would benefit from them and  so the decision by the FDA to allow for  over-the-counter sale of some hearing  aids for adults specifically it seems  like this is going to really spur  Innovation and prompt more investment in  this space it's also already allowed for  cheaper hearing aids to enter the market  the White House said recently that there  are several options now available at  Major pharmacies and other retailers who  are selling hearing aids that cost under  a thousand dollars in some cases under  eight hundred dollars which is a lot  more affordable than was available in  the past for Apple what will this study  mean for them yeah it's interesting I  mean Apple has definitely been getting  more into the healthcare space and it  seems like over the last few years  they've definitely made an effort to  roll out more accessibility functions  the hearing loss experts I've been  speaking to they're very excited about  what companies like apple could do to  really bring exciting new better  products into for instance the hearing  aid space so I guess we'll just have to  see whether or not a study like this  will  compel Apple to put more resources into  this space all right that's our reporter  Dominique mossbergen thanks so much for  joining us Dominique thanks Harry and  that's it for today's Tech news briefing  if you want more Tech stories head over  to our website wsj.com I'm Zoe Thomas  for The Wall Street Journal thanks for  listening  [Music]  [Music]

